DATA LICENSE NOTICE

The MIT license above covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository and NOTHING
ELSE. It grants no rights in any data, in any model, or in the Sciweon name.
A permissive code license does not make the data permissive.

DATA IS NOT COVERED BY THE MIT LICENSE. Data rights can vary by SOURCE, by
RECORD, by FIELD, by CONTRIBUTOR, by how a value was TRANSFORMED, and by the
FORM in which it is OUTPUT. There is no single license that describes
"Sciweon data", and this notice does not create one.

WHAT HAS ACTUALLY BEEN ADJUDICATED

A specific, frozen set of 25 rights-bearing FIELDS across three planes. These
are field-level determinations. A source named below is qualified FOR THOSE
FIELDS ONLY; it does not mean the whole resource carries that class.

  FIELD-QUALIFIED PUBLIC -- 5 named PubChem fields.
    Field-qualified, not a blanket public-domain grant. NCBI states it has no
    rights to transfer to a third party for contributed content, and
    depositor-provided fields may carry their own terms. No unconditional
    clean-commercial grant is asserted for PubChem as a resource.

  SHARE-ALIKE -- 14 named ChEMBL fields.
    ChEMBL is distributed by EMBL-EBI under CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported. Attribution
    and share-alike attach to distributed derivatives.
    NOTE, AS AN OPEN QUESTION AND NOT A CONCLUSION: CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported
    licenses copyright; whether and how the EU/UK sui generis database right
    in the underlying database is engaged has NOT been determined here and is
    referred to qualified counsel. Nothing in this file should be read as a
    legal conclusion on that point, in either direction.

  BIBLIOGRAPHIC -- 6 named PubMed fields.
    Attribution required; no license granted. NLM additionally requires
    republishers to state clearly when data does not reflect the most current
    NLM data.

  NOT IN ANY APPROVED OUTPUT PLANE.
    UniProt and UniChem. Gate-5B placed no field of either into an output
    plane, so nothing from them is approved for publication. This is an
    adjudication about what MAY be published; see the enforcement note below
    for what is actually prevented at runtime, which is a different and
    narrower thing.

ANY SOURCE OR FIELD NOT IN THE ADJUDICATED SET IS UNRESOLVED, and must be
treated as restricted rather than assumed open. This explicitly includes
sources that may look open at the resource level -- among them PubChem
BioAssay, ClinicalTrials.gov, openFDA, RxNorm and OpenAlex. Their overall
posture has not been adjudicated field by field, and a resource-level
impression is not a rights determination.

Where a previous version of this notice asserted a specific license for a
source without supporting primary evidence, that assertion has been WITHDRAWN
rather than replaced with a different guess.

WHAT THE RUNTIME ACTUALLY ENFORCES -- AND WHY THAT IS NOT THE SAME CLAIM

An ADJUDICATION is a determination about what may be published. An
ENFORCEMENT is a control that prevents publication. They are not the same,
and this notice keeps them apart deliberately.

The only rights control operating at runtime today is a limited MedDRA and
KEGG containment filter applied at the serving boundary. It is a denylist over
recognised shapes: an unrecognised source, a renamed field or a reshaped
payload is not caught by it.

There is NO runtime mechanism enforcing the 25-field approved set, and NO
runtime mechanism enforcing the UniProt or UniChem position. Those rest on the
adjudication alone.

This repository must not be represented as providing per-field rights
enforcement, and a reader must not infer a runtime control from the presence
of the approved-plane table above.

OBLIGATIONS ON CONSUMERS

Comply with the most restrictive applicable upstream terms for the SPECIFIC
FIELDS you use, and verify those terms against the upstream source rather than
relying on this file. Entity records carry provenance naming the originating
source; check it before any redistribution or commercial use.

NO WARRANTY AND NO FRESHNESS PROMISE

Sciweon makes no warranty regarding upstream data accuracy or completeness.
Original-source errors, retractions and corrections may not be reflected in
any given snapshot. Evidence responses report the snapshot date they were
served from; no refresh cadence is promised.

RESEARCH USE ONLY

Sciweon reports observed records with their provenance. It does not assess
causality, risk or clinical significance, and makes no clinical, diagnostic,
dosing or regulatory recommendation.
